      "writtenOn": "2023-08-07T18:00:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I commented above on why I think ConcurrentHashMaps probably wouldn\u0027t address this concern! I\u0027ve instead added the RW locks, with a write-lock being held while an interface is being added, and a read-lock being held while the indices are being consumed.\n\n----\n\nAn alternative that I considered was adding `synchronized` to getIfaceIndices and having getIfaceIndices return a _copy_ of the iface index set. This would have ensured that\n1) the iface indices could only be modified /or/ read at any given time\n2) the indices being read by getIfaceStats wouldn\u0027t change after being retrieved (since it\u0027s a copy)\n\nHowever, creating a copy of the iface index set for each call of getIfaceStats would probably be very expensive.",
      "parentUuid": "33011283_535688c7",
